<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH NOV MANUFACTURING SALES RISE TWO PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>DUTCH NOV MANUFACTURING SALES RISE TWO PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch November</p>
<p>manufacturing sales were some two percent higher than in the</p>
<p>same month of 1995, the Central Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The CBS manufacturing sales figures refer to the guilder</p>
<p>value of manufacturers' sales and are usually published one to</p>
<p>two weeks before manufacturing production figures which show the</p>
<p>rise or fall in volume terms.</p>
<p>DUTCH MANUFACTURING SALES</p>
<p>			  (pct change in guilders yr/yr)</p>
<p>			Domestic	 Export	  Total</p>
<p> November		    3		1		2</p>
<p> October		    13		9	     11</p>
<p> Q3 96			 6		4		5</p>
<p> Q2 96			 4		1		2</p>
<p> Q1 96			 1	     -2		0</p>
<p> YR 95			 5		8		7</p>
<p> YR 94			 3		6		5</p>
<p>The CBS noted that November 1996 had one fewer working day</p>
<p>than November 1995.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 570 8500</p>
</text>
